  {
   "c": "绍",
   "pinyin": "shào",
   "lectures": [
    "shào"
   ],
   "fr": "relier, continuer, présenter",
   "en": "to continue, to introduce",
   "parts": [
    "纟",
    "刀",
    "口"
   ],
   "nouveau": [],
   "sources": [
    "cjk-decomp"
   ],
   "role": "forme",
   "roles": {
    "刀": "forme",
    "口": "forme",
    "纟": "sens"
   },
   "origine_fr": "Le Shuowen jiezi glose 紹 par « continuer » : le fil, 糸, et 召 pour le son. Un fil qu'on noue au bout d'un autre, c'est ce qui continue et relie. Simplifié, 糸 devient 纟 ; 召, écrit 刀 sur 口, se lit zhào et ne donne plus le son de shào.",
   "origine_en": "The Shuowen jiezi glosses 紹 as “to continue”: thread, 糸, and 召 for the sound. A thread tied to the end of another is what carries on and connects. Simplified, 糸 becomes 纟; 召, written 刀 over 口, is read zhào and no longer gives the sound of shào.",
   "etiquette": "atteste",
   "memo_fr": null,
